WEBVTT

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.860
Come in.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.820
Miss, is this what you wanted?

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.240
Yes, thank you.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.320
What are you going to write about?

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.080
Well...

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.050
<b>July 20</b>

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.940
Hibari-chan, how'd you do?

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.010
It's about what I expected.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.560
So, summer vacation starts tomorrow.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.020
Take care of yourselves, at least 
until our outdoor school starts.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.520
"At least" until outdoor school starts?

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:13.900
This marks the conclusion
of your first semester.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.650
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.650
<b>July 20</b>

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.650
<b>Our Summer Vacation</b>

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.050
Twirl, twirl!

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.930
Botan, if you keep that up...

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.000
Botan-chan!

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:32.750
The... The squids are spinning...

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.690
I tried to warn you.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.710
Squids... Squids...

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:36.710
Are you okay?

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.410
For the time being...

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.590
Let's head over there.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:48.680
I'm sorry. A piece of human trash like me
doesn't even deserve to celebrate.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.850
Summit

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.180
Yoo-hoo!

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.120
Since summer vacation starts tomorrow,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:59.200
I was just thinking about doing 
this and that with all of you...

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.910
Then I started spinning.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.910
How embarrassing...

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.870
Everyone spins when they're 
having fun. Around and around!

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.960
You don't see it that often, though.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.080
What's wrong?

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.440
Oh, Ren-chan!

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.610
Don't just casually call her Ren-chan.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.000
Hibiki-chan's here, too!

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.480
I told you not to call me Hibiki-chan...

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.880
What are you doing?

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.720
It's a bit hot, so we're taking a break.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.160
A break?

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.570
Y-Yeah.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.880
Would you like to join us?

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.550
<b>Karaoke Coupon</b>

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.530
Wow! Karaoke?!

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:42.990
Karaoke?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.960
Um... Er... P-Please take this, if you like!

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.580
Yesterday, a blushing female
karaoke box employee

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.290
dared to give this to Ren.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.960
I want to go! I want to go to karaoke!

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.170
Since she offered, why don't we go?

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.500
Huh?

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.620
Um...

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.700
Are you afraid to go because you're 
worried that my wretched singing

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.340
will make your ears bleed?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.640
Of course not!

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.780
You're a monster...

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.610
I said I wasn't!

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.070
It's just...

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:24.630
I've, um... never gone to karaoke.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.220
Then it can't be helped.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.820
I, Hibiki, master of karaoke, 
will have to teach you myself.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.420
Hooray! Let's go!

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.690
Come on, let's go, Hibari-chan.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.170
U-Um...

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.410
Wait for me!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.170
<b>Festival</b>

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.170
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:46.130
<i>I can't go wrong with my map!</i>

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:47.140
<b>Karaoke</b>

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.730
<i>Knock, knock on the map in my mind</i>

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.740
<i>I'll leap out into the world</i>

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:57.040
<i>Map, map, knocking in my mind</i>

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:06.270
<i>The door won't open even 
the smallest, tiniest bit</i>

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:12.460
<i>My map must be taking the day off</i>

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.460
She really is quite good.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.880
Yeah. The melody feels kind of nostalgic.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.450
Well? What do you think of my singing?

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.100
You're supposed to applaud!

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.210
Botan, do you come to karaoke often?

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.420
Come on, applaud! Not enough applause!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:23.420
No, this is actually my first time 
at an actual karaoke box.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:28.140
There is a singing facility in my house
that I use sometimes, though.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.670
A facility?

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.860
Yes, we have various other facilities, as well.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.530
All of you should come visit.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.980
Tomorrow, then!

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.480
What? Tomorrow?

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.360
Yeah. Tomorrow.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.510
Okay, great!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.070
Well, I guess...

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.070
Hey, you're not listening to me sing!

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.360
You're next, Hibarigaoka Ruri.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.040
What? A-Already?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:03.070
<i>How are you?</i>

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:11.140
<i>I wanted to tell you last night 
that the stars were beautiful...</i>

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.520
Th-Thanks.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.220
Hibari-chan, you're a good singer!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.800
Why were you worried? You sing just fine.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.840
You have a beautiful voice, Hibari-san.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:28.330
I don't know a lot of modern songs.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.710
This was something I used to listen to a lot...

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:32.660
On a CD?

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.160
No, my mother often sang it while gardening.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:42.130
I didn't know what it was called, 
but I found it by searching for the lyrics.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:46.150
Really? It was wonderful, Hibari-san.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.170
Th-Thanks.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.800
Okay, I'm next!

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:54.060
You can do it, Hanako-san.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:59.060
<b>Screeeeech</b>

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.160
What is this? My ears...

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.560
Botan, hang in there!

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.840
It's audio feedback from the mic.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.220
But she hasn't even started singing,

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.310
and she's not standing near the speakers!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.450
I still couldn't do it...

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:14.710
Huh?

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:23.420
<b>Waaah!</b>

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.760
At every karaoke place I've been to,

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:23.420
the mic starts screeching the second I touch it.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.910
Hey, girls. You seem to be
having fun together.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.160
Timothy!

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.500
What are you doing here?

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.820
Since we won't be seeing 
each other for a while,

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.260
I thought I'd say goodbye.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.010
We won't?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:40.320
I'm scheduled for a maintenance 
check over summer vacation.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.480
Like a routine exam at the doctor?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.470
A-Timothy!

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.230
Here's a song to send you off.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:50.280
Timothy! Timothy! Timothy!

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:48.660
<i>Hey!</i>

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:52.470
<i>Ti-Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo, Timo, 
Timothy, feeling so happy</i>

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:56.260
<i>Ti-Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo, Timo, 
Timothy, having so much fun</i>

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.330
Ti-Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo, Timo...

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:58.330
Stop that!

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.800
Ti-Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo, Timo, extend our time!

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.210
We're not doing that!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.720
"Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo..."

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.440
With Timothy-san's impressive rap,

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.400
we concluded our karaoke contest.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.350
<b>Buzz
Buzz Buzz</b>

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.350
<b>Chirp
Chirp
Chirp</b>

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.310
The cicadas sure are loud.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:24.220
Again...

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:25.270
What's wrong?

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:30.980
Ever since we did karaoke yesterday,
I've had Timothy's rap stuck in my head.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:34.240
The "Ti-Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo" song?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.100
Don't! You'll make me remember it again!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:41.250
Maybe you could forget Timothy's 
song with another catchy song.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.250
Like what?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:47.540
Like the "Tasty, tasty!" 
song from the commercials.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.300
Now that one's stuck in my head.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.800
Then how about that 
"Red Mold Man, Blue Mold Man,

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.800
Black Mold Man, beat them all!" song?

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.780
Now it's that one!

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:04.110
But nothing beats "Ti-Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo," huh?

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.310
I said stop!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.490
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.020
Bye-bye!

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.900
She seemed afraid to look at me.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.330
Was my expression that scary?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:35.010
No, you were your usual self.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:37.930
Really? Then I wonder why...

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:42.310
Ugh, this is all because of Timothy's rap.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.910
The ocean!

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.400
It's amazing...

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.100
Yes.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.680
Hibari-chan! Look, look!
A crab! Check it out!

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:05.540
Pinch!

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.680
Hanako...

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.080
Seagulls, seagulls, seagulls,
seagulls, seagulls!

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.470
Anyway... I'm surprised.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:21.050
I can't believe all of this is man-made.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:24.780
My younger sister had this facility made for me

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:28.440
since I'm unable to go a real beach,

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.780
but it's too big for me alone.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.450
So I'm glad I was able to invite all of you.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:39.150
So you have a younger sister?

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.660
Y-Yes.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:46.920
Unlike me, a costly, troublesome girl 
lower than a rock on the roadside,

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.480
she's an athletic and cheerful girl...

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.170
Okay, I get it.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:55.920
I caught something.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:02.250
<i>It's like a real ocean in the water, too.</i>

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.120
<i>Let's race to that spot.</i>

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:07.770
<i>Sure.</i>

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:14.840
<i>I can't breathe...</i>

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.620
<i>All right!</i>

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:17.770
<i>I've won this one!</i>

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.610
Oh, good. You've regained consciousness.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.670
What in the world happened to me?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.420
You lost consciousness while swimming,

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.630
but Ekoda-san's resuscitation
skills were impressive.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.580
What? Resuscitation?

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.800
D-Do you mean...

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.690
Don't go to sleep!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:52.760
Strike.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:53.660
That's a hit!

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:54.690
Game, set!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.660
Once Ren-san awoke,

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.650
we had fun splitting a watermelon together.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:02.650
Oh!

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.120
Hee hee hee...

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.120
I actually wrote that.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:11.000
Summer 
Festival

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:10.250
Our next outing will be the town festival.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.910
<i>How are you?</i>

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:31.130
<i>I wanted to tell you last night 
that the stars were beautiful</i>

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.120
There.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:37.890
<i>Somewhere in this town</i>

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:44.860
<i>I want you to look up at the same sky</i>

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.770
I'm off!

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:52.730
<i>Even if I'm only talking to myself, that's okay</i>

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.530
<b>Fireworks Display</b>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:59.220
<i>I'll just write a letter in my heart, and erase it</i>

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:04.400
<i>Since I have no one to send it to</i>

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:09.600
<i>I'll quietly make it a paper airplane</i>

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.580
Thanks for waiting!

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:19.230
Hanako, you're right on time.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:23.240
Yeah! I only fell in the river once today.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:23.240
Splash!

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:26.150
But you did fall in...

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.720
Let's meet here if we get split up.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.120
Good idea. Shall we start
by browsing the stalls?

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:33.160
Okay.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.870
When did you get a grilled squid?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.860
<b>Candied Apples</b>

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:57.710
<b>Cotton Candy</b>

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:59.960
<i>Look right, look left, and take off!</i>

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:07.120
<i>Then I thought, "What?" By the time 
I reached this garden, it was too late</i>

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:12.540
<i>I've been going around in circles all this time</i>

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:09.590
<b>Chocolate 
Bananas</b>

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:10.780
You're not getting away!

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:19.640
<i>But that's to be expected, because 
Earth is going around in circles, too</i>

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.750
Glare...

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.110
Go away! Go away!

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:39.100
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.950
Huh? Where are Hibari-chan and the others?

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.090
Did we get left behind?

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:39.100
Let's try going to the meeting place.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:41.560
Yeah...

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.920
Let's eat that next!

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:44.570
<b>Festival</b>

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.570
Don't you have enough already?

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.150
I'd like to get it right at least once.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.200
Me, too.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.860
Huh? Where are Hibiki and Hanakoizumi-san?

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:54.990
<b>Stab</b>

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:05.380
What's wrong with them?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:09.090
We kept our word and came to wait for them.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.350
Hey, that was...

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:12.760
Huh?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:13.930
Timothy!

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:17.390
Huh?! Hey, wait! We'll get separated!

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:21.550
I said wait!

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:22.100
Wait!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.270
Timothy? Huh?

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:29.230
Just leave him alone. 
Let's head back to the front gate—

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:30.640
Hibiki-chan, this way!

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:33.760
Darn it, would you listen to—

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.030
<b>Whoosh</b>

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.040
D-Don't leave me alone!

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:43.120
Wow, so this is what the 
school looks like at night.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.540
I've never done this before.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.190
Me neither.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.630
Okay, let's leave. Let's leave right now.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.150
I thought I heard Hibiki's voice just now.

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.850
What? From where?

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.420
Over there, I think.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.930
Shall we check it out?

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:05.270
O-Okay.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.270
Something might jump out at us.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.720
Hibiki-chan, are you okay?

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:15.420
D-Don't be stupid! If you think 
I'm scared, you're dead wrong!

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:17.790
What? You're scared, Hibiki-chan?

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.400
I told you, I'm not the slightest bit—

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.340
Oh, good! Let's check 
out this classroom, then.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.460
H-Hey!

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:29.460
The work of an evil spirit?

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:31.210
<b>Click</b>

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:32.470
<b>Click</b>

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.720
<b>Click
Click
Click</b>

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.320
The lights don't work!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.510
Okay, I'll use this.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:51.550
Wow, there are lots of old man dolls.

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:53.280
Wh-What the heck are these?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.740
<b>First Principal Horikawa Shozo</b>

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.740
Looks like they're statues
of former principals.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:59.660
There sure are a lot.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.910
It's cute how they're all smiling slightly.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:07.380
<i>R-Really? I can't see what's cute about that...</i>

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:11.640
<i>Look, they seem like they
might say hello at any time.</i>

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:13.300
<i>I've had enough! Let's get out of here!</i>

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.580
What in the world is this?

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:26.190
Maybe a prop for the school festival.

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:30.620
Oh, my! The muscle extending 
from the cheekbone to the mandible

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.580
makes him seem like a jovial fellow.

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:35.900
That's enough! Let's head back to the gate!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.570
They're probably waiting for us there.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.870
Someone's singing?

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:43.100
Really?

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.080
Do you hear something?

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:50.460
Yeah. It's a kind of nostalgic 
song that stirs my heart...

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.450
Scary... So scary...

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.970
The seventh principal was a woman.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.800
What good will learning 
about past principals do?

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:01.930
Let's head back to the front gate.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.240
What was that voice?

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:07.520
Huh? I didn't hear anything.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:10.400
No, I heard it! I definitely heard something!

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:14.620
Maybe the principals said something.

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:17.850
P-Please stop saying things like that!

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:19.360
Huh?

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.330
On top of being scary,
it's making my head feel fuzzy.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:26.290
Speaking of armor....

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.840
There's a legend about a 
bloodthirsty suit of armor

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.250
that would attack tourists 
who came to a castle.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:38.350
At night, the armor took the bloodstained 
clothes of the tourists it attacked

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:43.540
and cheerfully counted them, piece by piece.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:47.730
Stop! That's not even how the story goes!

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.690
I've heard a similar tale.

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:55.870
During the Warring States period, 
the helmet of a warrior from Yamanashi

00:18:55.870 --> 00:19:02.660
who allegedly died in battle
suddenly flew into the air and said...

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:05.370
"She sells sea shells by the sea shore."

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:07.850
"By the sea shore."

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.900
"By the she shore."

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.450
"By the tea shore."

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:17.720
Timo, Timo, Ti... Ti... Ti...

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:20.470
Timo, Timo, Timo-mo-mo-mo
Timo-mo-mo-mo Timo!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.470
Enough!

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.050
Is that...

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:28.650
That's Timothy's rap! Timothy!

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:30.230
Hey, wait! Don't leave me behind!

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:33.940
This way!

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:36.940
Hanako!

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:40.900
Oh, you're all here! Hey, isn't this song...

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.660
It's Timothy, right?

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:46.640
<b>Ti         Ti</b>

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:46.640
<b>Ti         mo</b>

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:46.230
Are we really going in there?

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.080
Let's go.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:20:01.880
How?! Why are we hearing Timothy's 
voice when he's in pieces?!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:02.720
I'm not sure.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.120
Heave-ho...

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:12.140
Evil spirits, begone! Evil spirits, begone!

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:12.140
It's chasing us!

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:13.470
Wait for me!

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:14.350
Botan!

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:14.350
Botan-chan!

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:19.770
No fair! I want to be carried, too!

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:21.960
It's Timothy's legs! Legs, legs, legs!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.960
My legs are running!

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.880
Speaking of bits and pieces,
I heard a story once.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:36.540
Ten years ago, a young 
shepherd in some county...

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.500
Huh? What? What is it?

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.420
Legs, legs! It's Timothy's legs!

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:40.970
Legs, legs!

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:43.500
Every night he'd eat hotpot alone.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:46.240
Hotpot? Does that mean it was winter?

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.090
Please don't talk about that right now!

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:52.030
One day he realized he'd eaten 
all the meat in the pot.

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:53.770
He must've been a big eater.

00:20:59.390 --> 00:21:02.360
Ren! Carry me, too!

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:08.320
Darn it! Stop singing!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.690
What was that?

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:18.650
He was rapping even though his 
body had been taken apart.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:21.300
Let's forget it. I don't want 
to think about it anymore.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:23.260
It was fun, though, huh?

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:26.680
Yes. It'll make a good memory.

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.600
There's no way!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.340
The fireworks started.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.840
They're beautiful.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:05.580
Ti-Ti-Timo, Timo...

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:09.340
Summer vacation sure is fun.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:27.310
Standing before the giant fireworks,

00:22:27.310 --> 00:22:30.880
I engraved my summer vacation 
memories into my heart.

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:32.100
Miss.

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:35.120
It's ready.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:36.200
Thank you.

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:44.070
I hope I make lots of memories 
at tomorrow's outdoor school, too.

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:44.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:44.020
<b>August 18</b>

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:44.020
<b>A Stormy Outdoor School</b>

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:47.020
<b>Don't miss
the next
episode...</b>
